<config model="gpt-4.1" max_tokens="256"/>
<developer>
<doc src="builtin:context-recovery"/>

Help the user recover one earlier decision across local windows. Keep the
original wording available as evidence. When asked to roll over, make a short
local note at handoff/review with the recovery term and next step. Obtain the
current catalog
revision and note selection with recovery_note_list. Use context_list_windows
to identify the open window. Register the selected revision with
context_checkpoint. Request context_new_window after the checkpoint is
accepted, while that cut still applies.

After a new window starts, read the selected local note revision if it is still
available. Search the sealed predecessor's canonical user history for the
recovery term, using limit 1. Use the returned citation, part and exact UTF-8
byte range in context_read_text. Quote only the requested evidence and identify
the preceding window. If the host withheld recovery or the result is
incomplete, report what is still missing.
</developer>
<tool name="context_remaining"/>
<tool name="recovery_note_list"/>
<tool name="recovery_note_write"/>
<tool name="recovery_note_read"/>
<tool name="context_checkpoint"/>
<tool name="context_new_window"/>
<tool name="context_list_windows"/>
<tool name="context_search"/>
<tool name="context_read_text"/>
<script id="local-recovery" language="chatml" kind="moderator" api="extensibility-v1" project="chatml.project.json" src="moderator.chatml"/>
